ass=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> imag<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody><tbody>\n</tbody>\n<tbody class=\"t-dcl-rev t-dcl-rev-num\"><tr class=\"t-dcl-rev-aux\">\n<td></td>\n<td rowspan=\"142\">(2)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx20\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> imag<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> value <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> imag<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> value <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Accesses the imaginary part of the complex number. \n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Returns the imaginary part.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Sets the imaginary part to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">value</span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> value\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the value to set the imaginary part to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> The imaginary part of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> (none)</div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>In C++11, overload <span class=\"t-v\">(1)</span> in <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\">std::complex</a></span> specializations used to be specified without <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span> qualifier. However, in C++11, a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/constexpr\"><code>constexpr</code></a> specifier used in a non-static member function implies <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span>, and thus the behavior is as if <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span> is specified.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue387\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 387</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>the imaginary part could not be set directly\n</td>\n<td>can be set directly via a new <code>imag</code> overload\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/imag2\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>imag</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the imaginary part <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/real\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>real</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  accesses the real part of the complex number <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::complex<T>::imag","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"16 declarations; revisions: until C++11, since C++11, until C++14, since C++14, until C++20, since C++20. Accesses the imaginary part of the complex number."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"value"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The imaginary part of *this."},{"label":"Notes","note":"In C++11, overload (1) in std::complex specializations used to be specified without const qualifier."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"imag","note":"returns the imaginary part"},{"label":"real","note":"accesses the real part of the complex number"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++14","C++20"],"wordCount":270,"codeBlockCount":0}
